her free game you should know  of  is one you'll need to play for a long  time to receive everything for free but  it is possible  let me explain capcom arcade stadium is  a hub  where a host of their arcade games from  the 80s and 90s  are kept at face value everything does  cost money  not much but it is there well it's  possible to slowly build up this entire  arcade back catalog  for free right now the hub can be  downloaded which includes the warplane  game  1943 and capcom have confirmed further  promotions are planned  especially on ps plus for example last  month  ghosts and goblins was free to download  but that vanished before i was able to  share the news  i'll continue to monitor it and shout  out each month when something is added  for free  so if your dad tells you about how great  the arcades were in the 1990s  you can show him your digital arcade  capcom  arcade stadium is out right now on  playstation pc switch and xbox  whilst we're talking about free games a  quick note about one i told you about  last month knockout city  if you miss the 10 free days you should  know that they've changed their free to  play access  to allow anyone to play completely free  until they reach level 25  it's quite a lot of time i've got to say  definitely enough time to play without  having to shell over any cash  okay so that's four free games let's  call that two  and move back to full price games  [Music]  well actually a low budget game we have  a stadia exclusive which is now  releasing on ps4 pc and xbox  ox must die 3. i always saw this as a  game which inspired fortnite save the  world  setting up traps for oncoming waves of  orcs and surviving at  all costs box must die 3 is the natural  evolution to the series with new weapons  powers and of course traps if tower  defense games are your bag  ox must die 3 is worth your time july  23rd  if you're interested  next up samurai warriors 5. musu games  are still alive and thrashing  the core to this style of game 